Phase-49 / Slice 0002 — Latch Persistence (T1 BUG fix)
======================================================

Branch:   refactor/alert-engine
Base:     4cd7c39e (Phase-49/0001 closed)
Date:     2026-05-08

Goal: persist (rule_id, vehicle_id) → latched_at + last_fired_at +
fire_count_since_reset across pod restarts so once-mode rules don't
re-fire on deploy when their condition is still true.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-execution audit (Honesty Covenant rule 9)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Five drift items found between draft prompt and reality:

1. Wiring chain: prompt listed cmd/teslasync/main.go and
   internal/api/router.go as wiring targets. Reality: cmd/teslasync/main.go
   is a 71-line stub from Phase-47/04; all DI lives in internal/app/new.go.
   The alert evaluator is constructed inside
   internal/api/telemetry_handler_wiring.go via NewTelemetryHandler,
   which calls NewTelemetryAlertEvaluator(db,...) defined in
   internal/api/telemetry_alerts.go.

   Resolution: amended prompt's allowed-files to swap
   {router.go, main.go} → {telemetry_alerts.go, app/new.go}. The new
   set is minimum-blast-radius: telemetry_alerts.go constructs the repo
   internally from db (no signature change for callers), app/new.go
   adds the HydrateFromDB(ctx) call next to the existing
   LoadPrevSignalsFromStore loop.

2. Migration runner: prompt referenced goose. Reality: project uses
   golang-migrate via internal/database/database.go::runMigrations
   wrapped by `make migrate`. Amended prompt's verification block.

3. DB testing convention: prompt assumed integration tests against a
   real Postgres. Reality: codebase has NO pgxmock / testcontainers
   harness; the established pattern (per guard_repo_test.go,
   vampire_drain_repo_test.go, mileage_repo_test.go, signals_catalog_
   repo_test.go) is SQL-shape tests on exported `const`s. Behavioral
   tests for the repo's contract live in the engine integration tests
   via an in-memory fake satisfying the RuleStateStore interface.

4. Engine constructor signature: prompt suggested
   NewRuleEngine(stateRepo) — would have required updating ~30 call
   sites in rule_engine_test.go. Used setter pattern instead:
   NewRuleEngine() unchanged; SetStateRepo(repo) is optional. Tests
   that don't care about persistence pass nothing; production wiring
   in NewTelemetryAlertEvaluator passes the repo.

5. In-memory cache: prompt said to remove the in-memory OnceLatched
   bit entirely. Compromised: kept OnceLatched as a write-through
   cache of the persistent latched_at column. HydrateFromDB rebuilds
   the cache on boot; MarkFired writes DB-first then updates cache;
   ClearLatch updates DB then cache. Race-lost (MarkFired returns
   (false, nil)) updates the cache to reflect the persistent truth so
   subsequent eval short-circuits without another DB round trip. This
   gives us pod-restart safety AND keeps the existing test suite (~30
   in-memory-only test cases) untouched.

